  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A third-harmonic standing sound wave is formed in a pipe that is open at one end and closed at the other end. The length of the pipe is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.2\"></span> m. Point X is located <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> cm from the closed end of the pipe and point Y is located <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60\"></span> cm from the closed end of the pipe. What is the phase difference between the motion of a particle at point X and the motion of a particle at point Y?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{4}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
